proof.text:
Suppose the two displayed $\rho B$ equations in the last clause hold. Using Step 4 and functoriality of $z'^*$, their substitution gives
$$\begin{aligned}
\rho_{e''}B_{e,wz}
&=\rho_{e''}B_{e',z}\,z'^*B_{e,w}\\
&=\chi^z z'^*\rho_{e'}\,z'^*B_{e,w}
=\chi^z z'^*(\chi^w w'^*\rho_e)
=\chi^{wz}(w'z')^*\rho_e.
\end{aligned}$$
The last equality is Step 6. This proves exactly the conditional claim of the statement, without adding a new normalization or asserting the antecedents without proof.

